## Spaces for Sitcoms:

### Friends Apartment

-Fictitious layout with exterior shot in NYC, and interior shot at studios in California

Mismatch between interior and exterior. Also misrepresented what is typically attainable for a NYC apartment.

-Layout like a regular apartment, EXCEPT, missing fourth wall, so live audience can watch. The ceiling is also never shown, because it doesn't exist! Instead, lighting above simulates day, night, and even rain. "Flyaway" walls can be moved and adjusted for desired camera angles. The set designer included a "buffer" hallway between apartments served as a grounds for slapstick comedy: yelling, door slamming, etc. Behind the missing fourth wall can sit a massive audience. Between them is a zone for maneuvering camera and microphone equipment for filming.

